## Getting the embeddings

Whatever you built on v1.0 will now read v1.1 by just swapping the v1.0
embeddings for the v1.1 ones and re-running your downstream tasks.

The easiest path is the [geotessera](https://geotessera.readthedocs.io) Python
library. The freshly released [geotessera 0.9](https://github.com/ucam-eo/geotessera)
supports both v1.0 and v1.1 embeddings, so you can
select whichever version you need. There are new flags for `dataset-version` (pick 1.1 to upgrade),
and also a `dataset-variant`, since we have multiple parties now generating embeddings
for the community!

- The `cambridge` dataset-variant is run on our University servers and is a small-scale
  variant we are generating for early adopters of 1.1. Use this to try 1.1 immediately.
- The `default` dataset-variant will be a Zarr-native full global run of v1.1 run by
  [Cyclops.AI](https://www.cyclops.ai/) that will cover 2016-2025 for the whole world,
  and be hosted on AWS for cloud-native streaming access. We're still working through
  this run, so stay tuned for more news!

All the TESSERA embeddings (both v1.0 and v1.1) are now available in AWS Open
Data in the `tessera-embeddings` S3 bucket. The geotessera 0.9 release defaults
to using S3 to fetch the embeddings, which should be more reliable for everyone.
Lets however take a moment to remember the overloaded Cambridge University server
that bravely served embeddings for the first six months of TESSERA all by itself.
Thank you "okavango" for not crashing and taking all our embeddings with you!

## Running or fine-tuning the model yourself

If you'd rather generate your own embeddings or fine-tune on your own data, the
v1.1 weights are on Hugging Face:

- **[huggingface.co/geotessera/TESSERA-V-1.1](https://huggingface.co/geotessera/TESSERA-V-1.1)**
- **[huggingface.co/geotessera/TESSERA-V-1.0](https://huggingface.co/geotessera/TESSERA-V-1.0)**

There are checkpoints for both Microsoft Planetary Computer and AWS Open
Data preprocessing backends, so pick the one matching your data source.
Also do [let us know](https://eeg.zulipchat.com) if you generate embeddings so we can
sync up and perhaps add them to the global registry. More mirrors are always welcome.

